age_count) contains no locating message from her — but POL-NS-06 makes the fee refundable whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded, so her silence cannot restore the charge. The fare is arithmetically sound — the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), reconciling at difference 0.00 — so no separate fare defect under POL-NS-08(d) arises; the entitlement to move the charge fails for the arrival reasons above. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT); its absence is citable and it leaves the POL-NS-06(i) dwell-accumulation route unavailable to either side, though there are in any case no in-geofence intervals to sum.\n\nThe driver's request to hold the fee under POL-NS-09(b) is declined. That limb needs two admissible artifacts in direct contradiction that no clause resolves; the only tension here is between the driver-set arrival marker and the trace, and POL-NS-05 exists precisely to resolve it, while POL-NS-02 states the consequence of the missing in-radius fixes directly. No other escalation limb fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the counterparty-dispute counters are 0 and 0, the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4), and the deciding fact rests on an unimpaired artifact at weight 1.0.\n\nOutcome: the SGD 4.00 charged is refunded to the rider in full (fare_breakdown payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full, and it is not. Confidence 0.9, capped by the weight 1.0 of the GPS trace that carries the deciding fact."
